# Notation ratchet (PR #1188, R1188-U6 and R1188-U7;
# docs/links-notation-style.md).
#
# The ceilings on the links notation we own, per scope of
# data/meta/notation-rules.lino, measured by scripts/measure-notation.mjs
# (gate check-notation). Each count is of distinct items, so a new record
# that reuses existing keys moves nothing, while a new `_` name, a new
# abbreviated name, a new duplicated block or a new repeated field raises a
# count and fails the gate. The ceilings only fall: `--write` lowers them to
# the measure after a rule pass. `characters` is recorded for the concise-form
# passes and is not a ceiling, since new seed data rightly adds characters.
notation-ratchet
  scope data/meta
    underscore-names 3017
    abbreviated-names 202
    duplicated-blocks 9
    repeated-fields 86
    characters 1850173
  scope data/seed
    underscore-names 9506
    abbreviated-names 245
    duplicated-blocks 45
    repeated-fields 115
    characters 3532129
